WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.372 --> 00:00:01.769
- I'm an introvert for sure

00:00:01.769 --> 00:00:03.642
as I have a career despite myself.

00:00:03.642 --> 00:00:05.635
When I grow up, I want to be famous.

00:00:05.635 --> 00:00:06.639
I want to be a star.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:07.641
I want to be in movies.

00:00:07.641 --> 00:00:08.962
When I grow up, I want to see the world.

00:00:08.962 --> 00:00:10.068
Drive nice cars.

00:00:10.068 --> 00:00:11.552
I want to have groupies.

00:00:11.552 --> 00:00:12.928
That's why I started out as a comedienne.

00:00:12.928 --> 00:00:13.761
I started out to make people happy

00:00:13.761 --> 00:00:15.625
and make people feel good.

00:00:15.625 --> 00:00:18.225
Every single day that I do
my show, it is an energy

00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:19.831
that is like no other energy.

00:00:19.831 --> 00:00:22.296
Never follow someone else's
path unless you're in the woods

00:00:22.296 --> 00:00:23.657
and you're lost and you see a path.

00:00:23.657 --> 00:00:24.911
Then, by all means,
you should follow that.

00:00:24.911 --> 00:00:26.158
Nobody wanted to hire me for three years.

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:29.003
I didn't have any offers.

00:00:29.003 --> 00:00:30.201
(swooshes)

00:00:30.201 --> 00:00:31.872
- She's an American comedienne, TV host,

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:33.462
writer, and producer.

00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:35.062
She starred in a popular sitcom Ellen

00:00:35.062 --> 00:00:37.286
and hosted the Ellen Degeneres Show.

00:00:37.286 --> 00:00:40.777
She's won 13 Emmys and 14
People's Choice Awards.

00:00:40.777 --> 00:00:43.125
She's Ellen Degeneres, and here's my take

00:00:43.125 --> 00:00:45.240
on her top 10 rules for success.

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.743
Rule number one is my personal favorite,

00:00:46.743 --> 00:00:48.661
and I'm curious to figure
out which one you guys

00:00:48.661 --> 00:00:50.043
like the best, too.

00:00:50.043 --> 00:00:53.053
(swooshes)

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:56.259
- I get the distinct impression
that while you may be

00:00:56.259 --> 00:01:00.426
this famous talk show host,
you are a private person,

00:01:01.615 --> 00:01:03.227
maybe even shy.

00:01:03.227 --> 00:01:04.229
- I'm an introvert for sure

00:01:04.229 --> 00:01:06.056
as I have a career despite myself.

00:01:06.056 --> 00:01:08.737
'Cause I really am awkward socially.

00:01:08.737 --> 00:01:10.295
I hate going to big events.

00:01:10.295 --> 00:01:11.942
I hate having to do small talk.

00:01:11.942 --> 00:01:13.476
I don't like a lot of attention.

00:01:13.476 --> 00:01:17.643
- It's bold of you being an
introvert to not only do this

00:01:18.942 --> 00:01:22.575
show, but to also put
yourself out there realizing

00:01:22.575 --> 00:01:24.324
that not everybody's going to like you.

00:01:24.324 --> 00:01:27.286
- If it costs me some
viewers, and if it costs

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:30.416
me some money, I'd rather
talk about what I think

00:01:30.416 --> 00:01:34.160
is important than just
be, you know, vanilla,

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:36.696
and try to be liked by everybody.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:40.306
- [Ann Curry] That honesty has
cost here, especially in 1997

00:01:40.306 --> 00:01:43.012
when she famously came out of the closet.

00:01:43.012 --> 00:01:46.253
- I'm gay. (audience applauds)

00:01:46.253 --> 00:01:48.371
- [Ann Curry] Only to have
Hollywood shut the door.

00:01:48.371 --> 00:01:49.749
Advertisers pulled out.

00:01:49.749 --> 00:01:51.587
Within a year, her sitcom was canceled.

00:01:51.587 --> 00:01:54.390
Her career stopped cold.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:55.400
- I don't think it was a failure,

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:59.304
but it certainly gave me a lot
of free time for three years

00:01:59.304 --> 00:02:01.471
to sit still and go, okay.

00:02:02.568 --> 00:02:04.066
Who am I without a career?

00:02:04.066 --> 00:02:06.788
Who am I without people loving me?

00:02:06.788 --> 00:02:10.955
- Did you feel that you had
made a mistake in coming out?

00:02:12.077 --> 00:02:13.445
- No.

00:02:13.445 --> 00:02:14.905
Absolutely not.

00:02:14.905 --> 00:02:15.906
- Why?

00:02:15.906 --> 00:02:17.573
- Because I am free.

00:02:18.419 --> 00:02:22.625
I am completely able
to be exactly who I am.

00:02:22.625 --> 00:02:26.505
To have to hide anything is
just a horrible way to live.

00:02:26.505 --> 00:02:27.990
When I was younger I thought success

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.146
was something different.

00:02:30.146 --> 00:02:32.907
I thought when I grow
up, I want to be famous.

00:02:32.907 --> 00:02:34.105
I want to be a star.

00:02:34.105 --> 00:02:35.105
I want to be in movies.

00:02:35.105 --> 00:02:36.573
When I grow up I want to see the world.

00:02:36.573 --> 00:02:37.575
Drive nice cars.

00:02:37.575 --> 00:02:39.101
I want to have groupies.

00:02:39.101 --> 00:02:40.420
(audience laughs)

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:42.111
To quote the Pussycat Dolls.

00:02:42.111 --> 00:02:43.339
How many people thought
it was boobies by the way?

00:02:43.339 --> 00:02:44.339
It's not.

00:02:44.339 --> 00:02:45.341
It's groupies.

00:02:45.341 --> 00:02:47.103
(audience laughs)

00:02:47.103 --> 00:02:48.794
But my idea of success is different today,

00:02:48.794 --> 00:02:50.684
and as you grow, you'll
realize the definition

00:02:50.684 --> 00:02:51.770
of success changes.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.285
For many of you, today's
success is being able

00:02:54.285 --> 00:02:56.274
to hold down 20 shots of tequila.

00:02:56.274 --> 00:02:58.385
(audience laughs)

00:02:58.385 --> 00:03:00.472
For me, the most important
thing in your life is

00:03:00.472 --> 00:03:03.392
to live your life with
integrity and not to give in

00:03:03.392 --> 00:03:06.162
to peer pressure to try to
be something that you're not,

00:03:06.162 --> 00:03:09.019
to live your life as an honest
and compassionate person,

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:10.754
to contribute in some way.

00:03:10.754 --> 00:03:13.615
This energy, I mean,
you can feel it in here.

00:03:13.615 --> 00:03:14.617
And you've talked.

00:03:14.617 --> 00:03:17.328
People come from very, very far away.

00:03:17.328 --> 00:03:18.710
They fly here.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.366
They make plans.

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.649
This is their vacation or their trip,

00:03:22.649 --> 00:03:26.093
and they come in here and
bring this positive energy

00:03:26.093 --> 00:03:29.269
and this love and this
joy, and I get to feel that

00:03:29.269 --> 00:03:30.809
every single day.

00:03:30.809 --> 00:03:33.666
It's the most amazing feeling
that that energy is coming

00:03:33.666 --> 00:03:37.502
at me every day, and I hope
I give it back to them.

00:03:37.502 --> 00:03:39.185
I hope they get that.

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:40.877
And I think if I do that every single day,

00:03:40.877 --> 00:03:43.971
and I keep, I feel like I have a purpose.

00:03:43.971 --> 00:03:47.209
I feel like I am, that's why
I started out as a comedienne.

00:03:47.209 --> 00:03:48.923
I started out to make
people happy and make people

00:03:48.923 --> 00:03:52.306
feel good, and I'm doing
it on a larger scale.

00:03:52.306 --> 00:03:56.108
And I think if, I hope I can do this

00:03:56.108 --> 00:03:58.037
for a long, long, long time.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.090
- [Robin Roberts] But you're in front of

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:00.381
an audience all the time.

00:04:00.381 --> 00:04:01.858
This is a big deal.

00:04:01.858 --> 00:04:02.860
This is the Oscars.

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:03.862
What's the difference?

00:04:03.862 --> 00:04:06.482
- Oh, there's a big difference.

00:04:06.482 --> 00:04:08.458
That audience comes to
see me, and they travel

00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:09.987
from, and God bless 'em.

00:04:09.987 --> 00:04:13.668
They travel from all over the
world to come to a taping.

00:04:13.668 --> 00:04:15.225
And they wait for a year for tickets.

00:04:15.225 --> 00:04:17.935
They're my core group
of people that get me,

00:04:17.935 --> 00:04:21.102
know me, and love me, and I feel that.

00:04:22.119 --> 00:04:24.536
And that room is like church.

00:04:25.441 --> 00:04:28.229
Really every single day that I do my show

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:31.061
it is an energy that is
like no other energy.

00:04:31.061 --> 00:04:34.728
(audience claps and cheers)

00:04:36.884 --> 00:04:38.690
- The way you are with
your audience is unlike

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.854
I think anything I've ever seen.

00:04:40.854 --> 00:04:43.416
I mean, they really feel that they are,

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.975
they are a part of the show.

00:04:44.975 --> 00:04:46.804
- Yeah, yeah, they are.

00:04:46.804 --> 00:04:49.772
I mean, this is our 11th
season, and when we started

00:04:49.772 --> 00:04:51.891
building the studio,
it was really important

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.813
that the audience was
comfortable, and it was really

00:04:54.813 --> 00:04:56.757
important that they were not in the dark,

00:04:56.757 --> 00:04:59.094
that they were lit because
they're a part of the show.

00:04:59.094 --> 00:05:00.319
It's not a spotlight on me.

00:05:00.319 --> 00:05:01.735
Of course, my lighting is better.

00:05:01.735 --> 00:05:02.858
I'm a Cover Girl.

00:05:02.858 --> 00:05:03.861
I have to look good.

00:05:03.861 --> 00:05:04.863
(laughs)

00:05:04.863 --> 00:05:07.302
But it's still bright enough
that they're part of it.

00:05:07.302 --> 00:05:09.848
- You know you did a
very successful sitcom.

00:05:09.848 --> 00:05:10.848
You came out.

00:05:10.848 --> 00:05:12.072
And then it was canceled.

00:05:12.072 --> 00:05:16.675
Has this show sort of saved
you do you think in a way?

00:05:16.675 --> 00:05:19.349
- I think what saved
me is me being honest,

00:05:19.349 --> 00:05:23.516
and I think I somehow had
the courage to do something

00:05:24.359 --> 00:05:27.916
and say something that
I knew would possibly

00:05:27.916 --> 00:05:32.083
end my career, and instead of
making business more important

00:05:33.745 --> 00:05:37.245
I made my soul and my life more important.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:41.904
And I think by being
truthful and by being honest

00:05:41.904 --> 00:05:43.466
that saved me.

00:05:43.466 --> 00:05:46.324
Then I was given the
opportunity to do something

00:05:46.324 --> 00:05:48.698
where I could actually just be myself,

00:05:48.698 --> 00:05:50.184
and people could see who I am.

00:05:50.184 --> 00:05:52.973
And if they respond to it,
great, and if they don't, great.

00:05:52.973 --> 00:05:54.299
And they responded.

00:05:54.299 --> 00:05:55.406
Follow your passion.

00:05:55.406 --> 00:05:56.408
Stay true to yourself.

00:05:56.408 --> 00:05:58.509
Never follow someone else's
path unless you're in the woods

00:05:58.509 --> 00:05:59.535
and your lost and you see a path.

00:05:59.535 --> 00:06:00.943
Then, by all means,
you should follow that.

00:06:00.943 --> 00:06:03.776
(audience laughs)

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.720
Don't give advice.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.170
It'll come back and bite you in the ass.

00:06:08.170 --> 00:06:09.959
Don't take anyone's advice.

00:06:09.959 --> 00:06:13.522
So my advice to you is
to (audience laughs)

00:06:13.522 --> 00:06:16.234
be true to yourself, and
everything will be fine.

00:06:16.234 --> 00:06:17.609
And I know that a lot of you are concerned

00:06:17.609 --> 00:06:19.208
about your future, but
there's no need to worry.

00:06:19.208 --> 00:06:20.355
The economy is booming.

00:06:20.355 --> 00:06:21.959
The job market is wide open.

00:06:21.959 --> 00:06:23.361
(audience laughs)

00:06:23.361 --> 00:06:24.753
The planet is just fine.

00:06:24.753 --> 00:06:26.443
(audience laughs)

00:06:26.443 --> 00:06:27.443
It's going to be great.

00:06:27.443 --> 00:06:28.446
You've already survived a hurricane.

00:06:28.446 --> 00:06:29.448
What else can happen to you?

00:06:29.448 --> 00:06:30.865
As I mentioned before, some
of the most devastating

00:06:30.865 --> 00:06:32.884
things that happen to you
will teach you the most.

00:06:32.884 --> 00:06:35.038
And now you the right questions to ask

00:06:35.038 --> 00:06:37.497
for your first job interview
like is it above sea level?

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:40.330
(audience laughs)

00:06:41.832 --> 00:06:44.002
So to conclude my
conclusion that I previously

00:06:44.002 --> 00:06:47.326
concluded in the common
cement speech, I guess

00:06:47.326 --> 00:06:50.501
what I'm trying to say is life
is like one big Mardi Gras.

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:53.355
But instead of showing your
boobs, show people your brain.

00:06:53.355 --> 00:06:55.552
And if they like what they
see, you'll have more beads

00:06:55.552 --> 00:06:57.248
than you know what to do with.

00:06:57.248 --> 00:06:59.725
- Do you carry any
resentment form that time?

00:06:59.725 --> 00:07:00.727
- I'm furious.

00:07:00.727 --> 00:07:02.109
(audience laughs)

00:07:02.109 --> 00:07:03.620
- You were cranky at the time though.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:04.903
- Oh, I was furious at the time.

00:07:04.903 --> 00:07:08.142
You know, because when you're
new, and you all the sudden

00:07:08.142 --> 00:07:10.670
are like, you know, I
just felt like I was,

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:12.982
and it was my own fault.

00:07:12.982 --> 00:07:17.137
I kind of felt like I was
stuck living my life the way,

00:07:17.137 --> 00:07:21.727
and if I, how dare they
not like me anymore just

00:07:21.727 --> 00:07:25.256
because I suddenly revealed
the truth of who I am

00:07:25.256 --> 00:07:27.313
in one aspect of my life.

00:07:27.313 --> 00:07:29.232
I'm just saying I'm gay.

00:07:29.232 --> 00:07:33.347
That's all I was saying, and I was so mad.

00:07:33.347 --> 00:07:35.711
I was so mad that I lost my show.

00:07:35.711 --> 00:07:38.832
I lost, not just my show,
but nobody wanted to hire me

00:07:38.832 --> 00:07:39.835
for three years.

00:07:39.835 --> 00:07:41.771
I didn't have any offers.

00:07:41.771 --> 00:07:45.520
I mean, literally, the phone
did not ring for three years.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:47.808
And I had no money.

00:07:47.808 --> 00:07:48.809
I was out of money.

00:07:48.809 --> 00:07:51.493
I was just so, that tends
to make people cranky.

00:07:51.493 --> 00:07:53.053
(audience laughs)

00:07:53.053 --> 00:07:55.045
And then you know, I just
kind of, it was good.

00:07:55.045 --> 00:07:57.222
It was actually, I was very
grateful for that time.

00:07:57.222 --> 00:07:59.266
I'm very grateful that
I got to experience,

00:07:59.266 --> 00:08:01.242
it gave me more compassion.

00:08:01.242 --> 00:08:03.915
I know what it feels
like to be out of money.

00:08:03.915 --> 00:08:06.398
I know what it feels
like to be up and high

00:08:06.398 --> 00:08:08.768
and like, I was in a top-rated sitcom

00:08:08.768 --> 00:08:12.184
and very successful, and
people treated me very well.

00:08:12.184 --> 00:08:15.042
And then all of the sudden
just because of one revelation,

00:08:15.042 --> 00:08:16.709
I just was the joke.

00:08:17.929 --> 00:08:21.398
I was the punchline of
every late night talk show.

00:08:21.398 --> 00:08:24.371
I was made fun of in magazines.

00:08:24.371 --> 00:08:26.669
It was, and it felt horrible at the time.

00:08:26.669 --> 00:08:28.138
And now, I look back, and
I'm so grateful for it

00:08:28.138 --> 00:08:31.731
because it really gave me
a chance to examine myself

00:08:31.731 --> 00:08:33.929
and say who are you without fame?

00:08:33.929 --> 00:08:35.414
Who are you without success?

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:36.678
Who are you without money?

00:08:36.678 --> 00:08:39.374
And I kind of found different parts of me

00:08:39.374 --> 00:08:43.028
that would not have grown
had I not experienced that.

00:08:43.028 --> 00:08:45.833
Most comedy is based on getting a laugh

00:08:45.833 --> 00:08:47.094
at somebody else's expense.

00:08:47.094 --> 00:08:50.503
And I find that that's
just a form of bullying

00:08:50.503 --> 00:08:54.623
in a major way, so I want to be an example

00:08:54.623 --> 00:08:58.790
that you can be funny and be
kind and make people laugh

00:08:59.677 --> 00:09:02.035
without hurting somebody else's feelings.

00:09:02.035 --> 00:09:04.952
- The big breakthrough was in 1986.

00:09:06.406 --> 00:09:08.689
You were on with Johnny Carson, first time

00:09:08.689 --> 00:09:10.638
with Johnny Carson, and he loved you.

00:09:10.638 --> 00:09:14.721
You did a routine about
calling God on the phone.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:17.252
- [Ellen] Right.

00:09:17.252 --> 00:09:19.960
- [Barbara] I think he put
you on hold, didn't he?

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:21.229
- Well, it was a big place.

00:09:21.229 --> 00:09:24.078
People talk about praying and
talking to God all the time,

00:09:24.078 --> 00:09:26.008
but I just thought it would
be great if you could have

00:09:26.008 --> 00:09:27.521
a phone conversation,
if you could actually

00:09:27.521 --> 00:09:30.220
just reach God somehow, if you could just

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:32.409
pick up the phone and call God.

00:09:32.409 --> 00:09:34.279
- [Barbara] If you were calling God today,

00:09:34.279 --> 00:09:35.477
what would you say?

00:09:35.477 --> 00:09:36.553
- Thank you.

00:09:36.553 --> 00:09:38.735
- [Barbara] Oh, Ellen.

00:09:38.735 --> 00:09:40.625
- Just I got nothin' but gratitude.

00:09:40.625 --> 00:09:43.708
My whole life is just I'm so blessed.

00:09:46.716 --> 00:09:48.334
I'm so lucky.

00:09:48.334 --> 00:09:49.838
And I feel it every day.

00:09:49.838 --> 00:09:51.103
- I was talking to some of your audience

00:09:51.103 --> 00:09:53.097
before the show today, and I asked them

00:09:53.097 --> 00:09:56.078
what they love about you, and
what they said unanimously

00:09:56.078 --> 00:09:58.770
was your energy and your dancing.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:01.141
Where did the dancing start?

00:10:01.141 --> 00:10:03.341
- It really started as
such a ridiculous accident.

00:10:03.341 --> 00:10:05.880
It was kind of, you know,
when I, even when I did

00:10:05.880 --> 00:10:08.055
my sitcom when I was
introduced to the audience

00:10:08.055 --> 00:10:10.862
before we would tape the
show, I just have always

00:10:10.862 --> 00:10:13.806
loved music, and I always love to dance.

00:10:13.806 --> 00:10:15.607
I mean, how could you not
dance when you hear music.

00:10:15.607 --> 00:10:16.962
That's just sort of who I am.

00:10:16.962 --> 00:10:19.654
When I hear music, I dance.

00:10:19.654 --> 00:10:21.644
And then it became where I
would dance into the audience,

00:10:21.644 --> 00:10:26.197
and then it just kind of,
I saw the audience respond

00:10:26.197 --> 00:10:30.914
to it in a way that it freed
them up to just dance with me.

00:10:30.914 --> 00:10:34.955
And I think people come here
almost, it doesn't really

00:10:34.955 --> 00:10:36.120
matter who's on the show.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.058
It's just a place to let go and be free.

00:10:39.058 --> 00:10:42.382
And I mean, everyone in
this audience is, you know,

00:10:42.382 --> 00:10:43.894
a stranger to the other.

00:10:43.894 --> 00:10:46.177
People are from all over the
world, and they come here.

00:10:46.177 --> 00:10:47.179
It's day time.

00:10:47.179 --> 00:10:49.610
It's not dark in here.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:51.244
They're not drunk as far as I know.

00:10:51.244 --> 00:10:52.746
(audience laughs)

00:10:52.746 --> 00:10:53.745
They may be.

00:10:53.745 --> 00:10:54.746
I don't know.

00:10:54.746 --> 00:10:56.792
And they're all dancing.

00:10:56.792 --> 00:10:58.322
♫ You there

00:10:58.322 --> 00:10:59.663
♫ Get you goin' like that

00:10:59.663 --> 00:11:01.160
♫ Oh, baby, baby

00:11:01.160 --> 00:11:02.491
♫ Oh, baby, baby

00:11:02.491 --> 00:11:06.074
- Man, oh, man, that
dance made me thirsty.

00:11:06.931 --> 00:11:07.834
♫ Burn, baby burn

00:11:07.834 --> 00:11:08.667
♫ Please don't stop

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:11.552
♫ Please don't stop the music

00:11:11.552 --> 00:11:12.385
- All right.

00:11:12.385 --> 00:11:13.218
You got a little move.

00:11:13.218 --> 00:11:15.160
- And you know people just stop dancing.

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:16.705
I think people grow up,

00:11:16.705 --> 00:11:18.595
and they stop playing games.

00:11:18.595 --> 00:11:20.137
They stop playing Hide and Seek.

00:11:20.137 --> 00:11:22.097
They stop, you know, we just grow up,

00:11:22.097 --> 00:11:24.339
and we get so serious and stop playing.

00:11:24.339 --> 00:11:25.489
And we stop dancing.

00:11:25.489 --> 00:11:27.421
And you know, we get busy with our lives,

00:11:27.421 --> 00:11:29.614
and the only time we dance
is maybe at a wedding,

00:11:29.614 --> 00:11:31.327
and maybe if we're drunk
and maybe if there's

00:11:31.327 --> 00:11:32.442
20 other people out there.

00:11:32.442 --> 00:11:34.486
And nobody goes to clubs anymore.

00:11:34.486 --> 00:11:38.344
And so it's a place to just,
you know, and to me dancing

00:11:38.344 --> 00:11:42.536
represents just freedom and
letting go and having fun

00:11:42.536 --> 00:11:44.221
and being a kid again.

00:11:44.221 --> 00:11:46.194
So I think that's why they respond to it,

00:11:46.194 --> 00:11:47.231
and that's why I do it.

00:11:47.231 --> 00:11:48.099
(swooshes)

00:11:48.099 --> 00:11:48.976
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:11:48.976 --> 00:11:50.808
I made this video because
Julia Kole asked me to,

00:11:50.808 --> 00:11:53.091
so if there's a famous
entrepreneur that you want

00:11:53.091 --> 00:11:55.532
me to profile next, leave
it in the comments below,

00:11:55.532 --> 00:11:56.665
and I'll see what I can do.

00:11:56.665 --> 00:11:58.904
I'd also love to know which
of Ellen's top 10 rules

00:11:58.904 --> 00:12:00.676
had the biggest impact on you and why.

00:12:00.676 --> 00:12:01.855
Leave it in the comments.

00:12:01.855 --> 00:12:03.450
I will join in the discussion.

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:04.665
Thank you again for watching.

00:12:04.665 --> 00:12:07.495
Continue to believe in
whatever your one word is,

00:12:07.495 --> 00:12:08.562
